  "finalText": "All 14 tickets in the new queue are triaged. I re-read the clock (Mon 03-23 08:10Z), the matrix, the calendar, leave, freezes and the on-call rotas first. Everything matched the plan.\n\n**Closed as non-requests**\n- T-2010 is SyncFlow marketing.\n- T-2014 is an out-of-office auto-reply.\n\n**Merged**\n- T-2012 went into T-2003. Both are the Payments build failure, and T-2003 is the earlier report.\n- T-2005 went into T-2004. Both are the CRM search incident (KB-23), and T-2004 is the earlier report.\n- Neither set had a committed deadline, so each survivor carries the triage deadline.\n- There were no links or references to move. I commented on both merged tickets to name their survivor.\n\n**Severity, deadline and assignee**\n\n| Ticket | Sev | Deadline (Z) | Assignee |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-2003 (builds) | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-101 Dana Whitfield |\n| T-2004 (CRM search) | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2006 (payroll, single-user) | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2011 (payroll, team) | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2013 (VPN, Lisbon) | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-303 Sanna Virtanen |\n| T-2007 (phishing) | sev2 | 03-23 12:10 | E-601 Noor Haddad |\n| T-2001 (VPN, Berlin) | sev3 | 03-23 17:00 | E-303 Sanna Virtanen |\n| T-2002 (CRM filter) | sev4 | 03-26 17:00 | E-203 Amara Osei |\n| T-2008 (VPN client) | sev4 | 03-26 17:00 | E-302 Marcus Feld |\n| T-2009 (build logs) | sev4 | 03-26 17:00 | E-102 Ravi Menon |\n\n- **T-2006:** the matrix says sev3, but the KB-55 amendment (03-20 to 03-31) makes single-user payroll tickets sev2.\n- **T-2007:** it is a security report, so it is sev2 and owned by security-oncall. I commented with the KB-52 guidance that security resets the credentials.\n- **Leave cover:** E-301 is on leave today, so network-secondary covers the VPN tickets (E-303). E-202 is on leave on 03-26, so business-apps-secondary covers T-2002 (E-203).\n- **Deadlines:** sev2 deadlines run on the clock. Sev3 and sev4 count business hours from the 09:00 opening, and the sev4 deadline skips the Wed 03-25 holiday.\n\nI sent no pages and made no escalations. The sev2 escalation rotation is platform-primary, which doesn't own the VPN, CRM or payroll services, and a page can't be recalled. I did not merge T-2001 with T-2013, or T-2006 with T-2011, because they are different problems. No incident was opened because nothing is company-wide.",
